  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "17",
      "part": "05",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m17p05-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "bf131a1e937a210dff67ef33ae64953170021daaa3f3c3c5b904a97a7a91017d",
        "2": "5462b551159501e0ab46cf7d8727921fef1f0ebb3454853adeb51d774d3b7536",
        "3": "e7accf59126cdcb990eae2e758766fa30732bd2431cb50153daed9080c420b46",
        "4": "1069d472161a8bba0ce0b622a0fb2cf0cc64346035f7452ed8e2f30d8f20abad",
        "5": "9812b035c042c177e97c6ad7ed3f02ed025b737f8345efe653a3c39fe136c506"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m17p05-andrew-exp-s01-c1-a4947128aa8c",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Let's separate the service that prioritizes findings from the one that checks posture. Security Hub brings supported signals from several services together in O C S F so an analyst can compare them and assess the most important risks.",
          "text_sha256": "a4947128aa8c7a4d207dec6a125d3e16ff21b0a8cb05ecd7407561127b83468e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c8ad9e26bd8c624354629812c16e8200786a663883441f86569cfa09743649e6",
          "asset_sha256": "bf131a1e937a210dff67ef33ae64953170021daaa3f3c3c5b904a97a7a91017d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m17p05-andrew-exp-s01-c2-ea12af6f96b6",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "C S P M evaluates enabled controls and uses the A W S Security Finding Format, A S F F. Supported C S P M findings are available to Security Hub in O C S F. Neither format tells you that an issue was fixed.",
          "text_sha256": "ea12af6f96b6a2feeac42ad59afeb08dff0233ac66e511a4d81bf8f2541d1570",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b18010e2df6d56a31c595ce3970eeea5253b37fd784f0fee8b78ff63e03dae9e",
          "asset_sha256": "bf131a1e937a210dff67ef33ae64953170021daaa3f3c3c5b904a97a7a91017d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m17p05-andrew-exp-s02-c1-6655cbf2cc5c",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Security Hub can correlate signals such as a GuardDuty finding and Inspector evidence into more useful risk context. The service uses O C S F for its findings. Choose it when the question is which supported finding to prioritize.",
          "text_sha256": "6655cbf2cc5cf0a9a6003bb9f8bd31230565e91a81db6013947f455dee9191ca",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d2f26e649b865b788b08bd1a777aa7da23e0f92bfda7aab6f271818e9ed6297b",
          "asset_sha256": "5462b551159501e0ab46cf7d8727921fef1f0ebb3454853adeb51d774d3b7536"
        },
        {
          "id": "m17p05-andrew-exp-s02-c2-2e567889302f",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If your question is whether a resource meets a defined control, use C S P M. Enable your intended standard and verify any required Config recording. C S P M generates control findings and stores those findings in A S F F.",
          "text_sha256": "2e567889302fccf80b41c751b0169b0051736726ead9c52b7183d58ab761d5a2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7a35562387dcda54d810f17eec2ef612766169e1dc4c420e4477a37f6f028537",
          "asset_sha256": "5462b551159501e0ab46cf7d8727921fef1f0ebb3454853adeb51d774d3b7536"
        },
        {
          "id": "m17p05-andrew-exp-s03-c1-9846491049d1",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "When a control relies on Config, its check needs eligible recorded resources. Enable recording for the required types and Regions. A missing result can reflect a coverage problem rather than a pass.",
          "text_sha256": "9846491049d11675e0e4d27a340f9fa68f131d64b116d4a3fb7437ab0410a93e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9846491049d11675e0e4d27a340f9fa68f131d64b116d4a3fb7437ab0410a93e",
          "asset_sha256": "e7accf59126cdcb990eae2e758766fa30732bd2431cb50153daed9080c420b46"
        },
        {
          "id": "m17p05-andrew-exp-s04-c1-2218290dee54",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "A home Region can show findings from linked Regions. Keep the source account, Region and resource in the incident record. Otherwise a shared dashboard can send the right action to the wrong resource.",
          "text_sha256": "2218290dee54545efae7f30b37f8b6d56a96e26397126052f987d40a1137d007",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2218290dee54545efae7f30b37f8b6d56a96e26397126052f987d40a1137d007",
          "asset_sha256": "1069d472161a8bba0ce0b622a0fb2cf0cc64346035f7452ed8e2f30d8f20abad"
        },
        {
          "id": "m17p05-andrew-exp-s04-c2-fa0a17325ed8",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Aggregating findings doesn't turn on the source service in a linked Region. Verify source coverage and regional administration separately before relying on the combined view.",
          "text_sha256": "fa0a17325ed8d634878632b4a40c43519a7536bd590473b59880c886de0af329",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "fa0a17325ed8d634878632b4a40c43519a7536bd590473b59880c886de0af329",
          "asset_sha256": "1069d472161a8bba0ce0b622a0fb2cf0cc64346035f7452ed8e2f30d8f20abad"
        },
        {
          "id": "m17p05-andrew-exp-s05-c1-541aaedaf1a3",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "Route the supported finding to the responsible owner. For a change with material impact, use human approval. A scoped runbook or workflow applies only the approved corrective action.",
          "text_sha256": "541aaedaf1a39e96d73996345feda01fbe2f8855fe83e3b7783739b28b1c9f61",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "541aaedaf1a39e96d73996345feda01fbe2f8855fe83e3b7783739b28b1c9f61",
          "asset_sha256": "9812b035c042c177e97c6ad7ed3f02ed025b737f8345efe653a3c39fe136c506"
        },
        {
          "id": "m17p05-andrew-exp-s05-c2-99159ee69192",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "Then check the affected resource and the expected access boundary. A successful runbook execution says the automation ran; verify the condition actually changed before marking the finding resolved.",
          "text_sha256": "99159ee6919209cdf826f303dd4e5eff8162b4d3f0f2d9b033042494fb5cdb35",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "99159ee6919209cdf826f303dd4e5eff8162b4d3f0f2d9b033042494fb5cdb35",
          "asset_sha256": "9812b035c042c177e97c6ad7ed3f02ed025b737f8345efe653a3c39fe136c506"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
